  "method": "Foot normal >1e-7 at 1.25 ms substeps, foot-contact runs bridge at most two silent substeps. In complete runs, compare first and last positive normal impulses for rear-toe two segments and front-toe six segments. Equal substep means unresolved order, not simultaneous biological contact. Group sums can mix toe segments and do not establish plantar identity or biological timing; thresholds and gap merging are engineering choices. Used development seed and 4\u20136 s only.",
